# Design system

Mood Taster should feel playful, pressable, fast, and clear.
Content first, controls second. Don't make me think. Let me react.

Product surfaces use a **gamified pressable** language (thick bottom borders,
outlined cards, soft shadows on primary cards). Marketing/docs pages may stay
quieter, but product chrome follows this file.

## Palette

| Token | Value | Role |
|-------|-------|------|
| `--paper` | `#fdfaff` | Ghost White. Main canvas ~80%. |
| `--ink` | `#510c85` | Indigo Purple. Primary brand / actions ~20%. |
| `--accent` | `#ffdf6e` | Royal Gold. Highlight, sparingly. |
| `--ink-deep` | `#310752` | Darker indigo for pressable bottom edges. |

Every neutral is a **mix of paper and ink**, never a new hue:

```css
--paper-muted: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 62%, var(--paper));
--paper-quiet: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 38%, var(--paper));
--ink-raised:  color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 7%, var(--paper));
```

Rules:

- Ghost White dominates. Screens stay bright and open, not purple-heavy
- Indigo for primary CTAs, active states, selected items, and brand moments
- Gold for a great match, special highlight, or tiny mark. Never a second primary
- If a screen feels colorful, we used too much color
- No status greens as a fourth brand hue. Reject hover may use a soft red tint
  on the X control only

## Shape language

```css
--radius-sm: 12px;
--radius-btn: 16px;
--radius-card: 24px;
--radius-lg: 24px;
--radius-xl: 32px;
--radius-pill: 999px;
--press-border: 2px;
--press-depth: 6px;
--press-depth-sm: 4px;
```

## Spacing (8px system)

```css
--space-2: 0.5rem;  /* 8 */
--space-3: 1rem;    /* 16 */
--space-4: 1.5rem;  /* 24 */
--space-5: 2rem;    /* 32 */
--space-6: 3rem;    /* 48 */
--space-7: 4rem;    /* 64 */
--space-8: clamp(4rem, 12vh, 7rem);
```

Most component spacing uses 16px or 24px. Give content room to breathe.

## Buttons (pressable)

- **Primary:** indigo fill, ghost text, thick bottom border `--ink-deep`,
  compress on `:active`
- **Secondary:** white fill, indigo text, indigo border + thick bottom edge
- **Icon:** white square, same press language, smaller depth
- **Highlight:** gold fill, indigo text. Special actions only
- Keep copy tiny (Show me, Taste my mood, Let's go)

Use `.cta` / `.cta-secondary` / `.press-btn` / `PressButton`.

## Icons

Teach the interaction. Prefer icon + 1–3 words. No emojis in product UI.

♡ like · × not for me · ↻ try again · ← → browse · ＋ add · ✓ confirm · ⌕ search

## Cards and result reactions

Cards are large, content-driven, often white with indigo border and a thick
bottom edge. Soft shadows are allowed on the main result card and key stat cards.

Result reactions: **X** reject / next, **♡ + CTA** accept (Let's go / Make this /
That's the one). No swipe required. Favor taps over forms.
Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.

## Quiz

Intent: full-width stacked pressable cards with descriptions.
Craving steps: **2-column icon grid** on all widths.

## Decorative motion

Floating decorative icons on landing / stats / profile are allowed.
Disable looping motion when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.
Screen entrance may use spring/fade via Motion. Prefer intentional motion
over ambient noise.

## Never

- No gradients as the main visual idea
- No emojis in UI
- No fourth brand hue for generic status
- Do not invent recipe content in Sous Chef chat

## Copy

Write for a third grader. Headlines 2–6 words. Body rarely over two short
sentences. No em dashes. User words: mood, taste, match, pick.

## Required exceptions

- `:focus-visible` outlines on every interactive element
- `box-sizing: border-box`
- Underlines on inline text links
- Monochrome `.grain` overlay (brand texture only)

## Sponsored placements

Label with type, not a badge box: accent eyebrow `Sponsored match` in `.eyebrow`
style. Never quieter than the organic label beside it.

## Checklist before shipping UI

- [ ] Ghost White dominates; indigo drives actions; gold is sparse
- [ ] Pressable borders/depth come from the system
- [ ] No emoji; icons explain actions
- [ ] One clear primary CTA per screen
- [ ] Copy stays short
- [ ] Focus states still visible on keyboard nav
- [ ] Reduced motion disables looping decorations
